    { "id": "guide-rows", "x": 2380, "y": 0, "w": 300, "text": "How to read this canvas\n\nRows 1–2: the child app (Sunrise theme, phone 390×844). Home is the entry screen; the celebration shows the moment after an approval.\n\nRow 2, last frame: an alternate palette (Night Sky) on the same layout, for comparison only.\n\nRows 3–5: the parent app (Slate theme, desktop 1440×900).\n\nBottom right: tokens and component states that Phase 3 builds from." },
    { "id": "note-night", "x": 2380, "y": 964, "w": 300, "text": "Night Sky is a token swap, not a redesign. Options: keep Sunrise as the only child theme, ship both with a child-selectable toggle, or use Night Sky automatically after the family's quiet hours." },
    { "id": "note-approvals", "x": 3040, "y": 1928, "w": 300, "text": "Approvals: the retry side sheet shows the child-facing tone. Parents never see a “Reject” button; the child never sees the word." }
